{
"start": 168.47,
"end": 192.0,
"text": "Five ideas. In PAM, the height is the sample; a sample-and-hold makes flat tops. In PWM, the width follows the sample, and one edge moves. PPM shifts a fixed pulse instead. Bandwidth rises from PAM to PWM to PPM: narrow pulses, big bill. And constant height lets the receiver slice at half height, so only edge jitter hurts.",
